<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Senate may vote telecom bill Thursday.</title>
<headline>Brazil Senate may vote telecom bill Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Senate may hold a floor vote Thursday on a bill paving the way for the privatization of the telecommunications industry after agreeing to make the law a priority, an official said.</p>
<p>The Senate official said 45 senators voted to give the so-called General Telecommunications Law fast-track treatment while 11 opposed the motion and three abstained.</p>
<p>The earliest date for a priority vote would be Thursday, he added.</p>
</text>
